SUMMARY:✅ Falcon 9 · Bandwagon 5 (Dedicated Mid-Inclination Rideshare)
DTSTART:20261020T110400Z
DTEND:20261020T120400Z
LOCATION:Space Launch Complex 40\, Cape Canaveral SFS\, FL\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Status: Launch Successful\nWindow: Tue\, 20 Oct 2026 10:30:00 U
 TC – Tue\, 20 Oct 2026 11:30:00 UTC\nWeather: 95% GO\nOrbit: Low Earth O
 rbit\nPad: Space Launch Complex 40\, Cape Canaveral SFS\, FL\, USA\n\n▶ 
 Watch live: https://x.com/i/broadcasts/1nxeLMddZlEJX\n\nDedicated rideshar
 e flight to a mid-inclination orbit with dozens of small microsatellites a
 nd nanosatellites for commercial and government customers.\n\nThis launch 
 also carries the second demonstration mission for SpaceX’s Project Starf
 all\, which aims to mass-produce reentry capsules designed to autonomously
  transport valuable customer experiments and other payloads safely back fr
 om space to Earth\, including for in-orbit manufacturing. \n\nStarfall is 
 a cylindrical shaped capsule approximately 0.75 meters tall with a diamete
 r of 3.1 meters\, weighing approximately 2100 kilograms\, and capable of c
 arrying 1000 kilograms of payload. It is designed to be carried on Starshi
 p flights.\n\nCountdown & updates: https://benjaminowens612.github.io/spac
 ex-launch-alerts/#3b430f81-0ff1-4d85-8a1a-cef0de326198
URL:https://x.com/i/broadcasts/1nxeLMddZlEJX
CATEGORIES:other
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
